# CocoIndex Code Search

## Purpose

Use CocoIndex only when its configured server or executable is present and the index belongs to the current checkout.

## Activation

Activate for broad or structural code discovery when direct symbol navigation is insufficient. Treat the index as generated data, not source. Confirm freshness using the index’s documented metadata or refresh procedure before relying on results.

## Workflow

Query the index for structural discovery, then verify important results against repository files and tests. Invalidate or refresh the index after changes that make its metadata stale, following the active tool’s documented procedure.

## Non-applicability

Do not activate for non-code tasks, narrow edits that do not need broad discovery, or repositories without a configured CocoIndex system.

## Fallback

If unavailable or stale, use Serena or targeted `rg` search. Do not invent refresh commands or claim index-backed evidence without a successful query.

## Control status

This is advisory guidance; it does not enforce index refresh, freshness, or query use.
